rulings.reasoning:
The plan's required-block set and geometry come from the deployed catalog folder next to RackCad.Application.dll. The folder is editable in place and its cache is keyed by name, size and mtime with no content hash (sa3b F8.3), and no current BUILD_BOUND field binds it. Conditions:
- the field covers the resolved directory path and every *.csv and *.json in it, matching the provider's signature scope, not only the 7 files;
- it hashes the deployed bytes (CRLF under autocrlf; D-08);
- it is sampled before acquisition and re-checked after CP.

rulings.recommendation:
ACCEPT with conditions:
(1) a pin (AR2-16), derived only from non-governing characterization defined in sealed scenarios (D-06), reconciled with V17 L-36/CT-50;
(2) scope limited to what no plan, writer constant or I-52 authority determines, which excludes the top-level reference's ST-13 set (D-07);
(3) keys are the consumed context variables (CLAYER, CECOLOR, CELTYPE, CELTSCALE, CELWEIGHT, CETRANSPARENCY, CPLOTSTYLE, text and dimension style records), captured in the PRE_COMMAND_STATE_RECORD;
(4) UNKNOWN (O5) while unpinned.

