votes.reasoning:
I tried to refute this item and could not. I re-read the files at worktree HEAD 1625a306 and checked every claim myself.

1. BA-05 V3 states the values that it says it does not hold. Line 821 says "The tolerance values live only in BA-08 V3 section 10 ... this section names the slots (AR2-35)". Yet the normative vectors restate them:
   - line 863 (SV-06): "TOL_LENGTH = 1e-9 in";
   - line 867 (SV-10): "TOL_ANGLE = 1e-9 rad";
   - line 868 (SV-11): "TOL_NORMAL = 1e-9 rad".
   gen.py lines 504, 506, 512 and 515 put the same texts into the JSON 'rule' fields. BA-08 V3 section 10's heading also says "BA-05 V3 names the slots only", and the vectors contradict it.

2. The vector results depend on those values. I decoded the hex:
   - SV-06: 4024000000044b83 - 10 = 5.0000004e-10;
   - SV-07: 4024000000112e0c - 10 = 2.0000002e-9;
   - SV-10: 401921fb543b9612 gives min(d, 2pi-d) = 5.0000004e-10;
   - SV-11: 3e212e0be826d695 = 2e-9, and atan2 gives 2e-9.
   EQUAL/DIFFERENT for SV-06, SV-07, SV-10 and SV-11 holds only while TOL_LENGTH, TOL_ANGLE and TOL_NORMAL are 1e-9 (for example, TOL_LENGTH = 1e-10 would flip SV-06). The vectors are labelled NORMATIVE, and the JSON status is "NORMATIVE (as part of BA-05 when sealed)". They have no tolerance input column, and nothing marks 1e-9 as a test parameter separate from the baseline value. So the artifact does not already handle the issue.

3. The dependency is real under BA-11 V3's own rule. Line 51 says "X depends on Y when a normative value of X is defined in Y". The normative results of SV-06, SV-07, SV-10 and SV-11 depend on values defined in BA-08 section 10. So BA-05 does depend on BA-08. BA-11 still declares:
   - BA-05 DEPENDS_ON = BA-01 plus the census only (line 64);
   - BA-08 DEPENDS_ON includes BA-05;
   - seal order BA-05 before BA-08 (line 54).
   The cycle that AR2-35 and BA11-F3 required to be broken is therefore still there, only undeclared. BA-05 would be sealed with results based on tolerance values that are not yet sealed. The cascade rule (line 37) would not re-open BA-05 if BA-08 changed a value.

4. The conformance check inherits the defect. BA-04 V3 Q-FPSPEC-VECTORS expects "every semantic result reproduced", and its authority is BA-05 3.3. Its FPSPEC_CONFORMANCE_TUPLE binds the BA-05 hash but not the BA-08 hash.

5. PA-9 ("if changed later, produce a new baseline") does not save it. PA-9 gives the values to the Selective kind baseline (BA-08). BA-11's cascade is the mechanism that carries such a change, and it is keyed on DEPENDS_ON, which is wrong here.

The TOL_SCALE row (line 829) restating "UNSET, no authority (K-3)" is a smaller, secondary part of the claim. It is also a restatement of BA-08 status that could go stale.

MAJOR is the right severity. The defect contradicts a closed Architect decision (AR2-35), makes BA-11's normative acyclicity and seal order false by its own definition, and reopens the substance of BA11-F3, which was MAJOR. The required fix is appropriate: write the four vectors in slot units, or move the numeric instances into BA-08, and change the TOL_SCALE row to point to BA-08.

